<div class="size-guide-page full-width">
  <!-- BREADCRUMBS -->
  <div class="size-guide-breadcrumbs-container">
    <div class="size-guide-breadcrumbs">
      <a href="/">HOME</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="current">RING SIZE GUIDE</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="size-guide-inner">
    <!-- PAGE HEADER -->
    <div class="size-guide-header text-center">
      <span class="size-guide-tag">Sizing & Measurement</span>
      <h1 class="size-guide-title">Find Your Perfect Fit</h1>
      <p class="size-guide-intro">Choosing the right ring size is important for a comfortable and secure fit. For the most accurate result, we recommend having your finger professionally measured by a jeweller.</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="size-guide-content">
      <!-- 1. MEASURE A RING THAT ALREADY FITS -->
      <div class="size-guide-card">
        <div class="card-header-with-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#c5a880" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <path d="M12 8v8"/>
            <path d="M8 12h8"/>
          </svg>
          <h2>Measure a Ring That Already Fits</h2>
        </div>
        <p>If you already own a ring that fits the intended finger comfortably, you can find your size in three simple steps:</p>
        <ol class="size-steps-list">
          <li><strong>Select the right ring:</strong> Choose a ring that is worn on the exact same finger and hand as your new piece.</li>
          <li><strong>Measure the diameter:</strong> Use a precise ruler or vernier caliper to measure the <em>inside diameter</em> (from one inner edge to the opposite inner edge at the widest point in millimetres).</li>
          <li><strong>Compare with the chart:</strong> Match your measured millimetres with the Ring Size Chart below to find your AU/UK size.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <!-- 2. RING SIZE CHART -->
      <div class="size-guide-card">
        <div class="card-header-with-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#c5a880" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <rect x="3" y="3" width="18" height="18" rx="2" ry="2"/>
            <line x1="3" y1="9" x2="21" y2="9"/>
            <line x1="9" y1="21" x2="9" y2="9"/>
          </svg>
          <h2>Ring Size Chart</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="table-subtitle">Australian and British sizes use letters (A–Z), while US sizing uses numbers. Use the inside diameter (mm) as your primary reference.</p>
        
        <div class="table-responsive-wrapper">
          <table class="size-chart-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>AU / UK Size</th>
                <th>US Size</th>
                <th>Inside Diameter (mm)</th>
                <th>Inside Circumference (mm)</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td><strong>H</strong></td><td>4</td><td>14.9 mm</td><td>46.8 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>I</strong></td><td>4.5</td><td>15.3 mm</td><td>48.0 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>J</strong></td><td>5</td><td>15.7 mm</td><td>49.3 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>K</strong></td><td>5.5</td><td>16.1 mm</td><td>50.6 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>L</strong></td><td>6</td><td>16.5 mm</td><td>51.9 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>M</strong></td><td>6.5</td><td>16.9 mm</td><td>53.1 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>N</strong></td><td>7</td><td>17.3 mm</td><td>54.4 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>O</strong></td><td>7.5</td><td>17.7 mm</td><td>55.7 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>P</strong></td><td>8</td><td>18.1 mm</td><td>57.0 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Q</strong></td><td>8.5</td><td>18.5 mm</td><td>58.3 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>R</strong></td><td>9</td><td>18.9 mm</td><td>59.5 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>S</strong></td><td>9.5</td><td>19.4 mm</td><td>60.8 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>T</strong></td><td>10</td><td>19.8 mm</td><td>62.1 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>U</strong></td><td>10.5</td><td>20.2 mm</td><td>63.4 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>V</strong></td><td>11</td><td>20.6 mm</td><td>64.6 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>W</strong></td><td>11.5</td><td>21.0 mm</td><td>65.9 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>X</strong></td><td>12</td><td>21.4 mm</td><td>67.2 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Y</strong></td><td>12.5</td><td>21.8 mm</td><td>68.5 mm</td></tr>
              <tr><td><strong>Z</strong></td><td>13</td><td>22.2 mm</td><td>69.7 mm</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="chart-footnote"><em>* International size conversions are approximate and may vary slightly between sizing standards. Inside diameter should be used as the primary measurement reference.</em></p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3. PRINTABLE RING SIZE GUIDE (PDF) -->
      <div class="pdf-download-card">
        <div class="pdf-icon-wrap">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="36" height="36" fill="none" stroke="#c5a880" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M14 2H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v16a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V8z"/>
            <polyline points="14 2 14 8 20 8"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="18" x2="12" y2="12"/>
            <polyline points="9 15 12 18 15 15"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="pdf-content-wrap">
          <h3>Printable Ring Size Guide</h3>
          <p>Already have a ring that fits? Print our official Ring Size Guide to place your existing ring directly over actual-size circles and confirm your perfect fit.</p>
          <a href="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0762/9615/9404/files/Arlena_Printable_Ring_Size_Guide.pdf?v=1784600164" class="btn-pdf-download" target="_blank" download>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-download" style="margin-right: 8px;"></i> DOWNLOAD PRINTABLE GUIDE (PDF)
          </a>
          <div class="pdf-alert-note">
            <strong>Important Printing Instructions:</strong> Ensure your printer is set to <strong>100% / "Actual Size"</strong> (do not select "Fit to Page" or "Scale to Fit"). Verify the 50 mm calibration line with a ruler before measuring.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- 4. SIZING TIPS & BEST PRACTICES -->
      <div class="size-guide-card">
        <div class="card-header-with-icon">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="#c5a880" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12" y2="12"/>
            <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12.01" y2="8"/>
          </svg>
          <h2>Sizing Tips & Considerations</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="size-tips-list">
          <li><strong>Dominant Hand:</strong> Your dominant hand is often slightly larger than your non-dominant hand. Always measure the specific finger where the ring will be worn.</li>
          <li><strong>Temperature & Time of Day:</strong> Fingers naturally swell in the evening and in warmer weather, while cold weather can cause them to shrink. Measure when your hands are at a comfortable room temperature.</li>
          <li><strong>Knuckle Consideration:</strong> If your knuckle is significantly larger than the base of your finger, measure both your knuckle and the base, then choose a size in between so the ring slides over smoothly yet stays secure.</li>
          <li><strong>Ring Band Width:</strong> Wider bands (over 4 mm) feel more snug on the finger than delicate, slim bands. If choosing a wide band design, you may want to go half a size up.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- 5. COMPLIMENTARY RESIZING & EXPERT HELP -->
      <div class="resizing-assurance-card">
        <div class="assurance-icon-box">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="32" height="32" fill="none" stroke="#c5a880" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <div class="assurance-text-box">
          <h3>Complimentary 30-Day Resizing</h3>
          <p>We want your Arlena piece to fit seamlessly. If your ring isn't quite the right fit upon arrival, we offer a <strong>complimentary first resize within 30 days</strong> of delivery on all eligible rings.</p>
          <div class="assurance-actions">
            <a href="/pages/contact" class="btn-ask-specialist">CONTACT OUR SPECIALISTS</a>
            <a href="/collections/engagement-rings" class="btn-shop-rings">EXPLORE ENGAGEMENT RINGS</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

